Fix a false negative for ``unused-import``: when a module imports two sibling
submodules of the same package (e.g. ``import pkg.a`` and ``import pkg.b``),
using one of them no longer hides the other one being unused. Both imports
bind the same local name (``pkg``), so using either one used to mark the
whole name as consumed, silently suppressing the warning for the sibling that
was never referenced.

Closes #2583
